A *[*^]* is used when the word has a special meaning in the context (like once before) or if you want to emphasize something (*"Once again I'll tell you what you already know."*) The same applies to the second usage of once in your example (*"Once again he went on to make things worse."*)

The third and fourth examples do not require a clarification, as the context is clear enough without one (*"Once more, the sun came up over the mountains."*)
*Once* with no *^* is the most commonly used form of the word and it means *in some previous occurrence*, which can be emphasized by adding an adjective (more, yet, ever, never, etc.)

